# Mix build output and fetched dependencies.
/_build/
/cover/
/deps/
/doc/
/.fetch
erl_crash.dump
*.ez
*.beam

# Cargo output for the NIF crate. Mix drives that build and copies the shared
# object into _build/, so nothing under target/ is ever an input to anything.
/native/aph_nif/target/

# The compiled NIF itself, which rustler also copies here. A shared object is
# build output twice over: it embeds absolute build-machine paths (the name
# hygiene scan catches them — that is how this entry got written), and a
# committed binary nobody can read is exactly the artifact a supply-chain
# reviewer cannot review. Every consumer builds it from source via mix.
/priv/native/

# ⛔ DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: `mix.lock` and `native/aph_nif/Cargo.lock`.
# Both are written by the first successful build, and both belong in the same
# commit as the code that caused them — the same rule the Python binding's
# workflow states about its own lockfile. Without them CI re-resolves the whole
# dependency tree on every run, and the version this binding was actually
# tested against is nowhere on record.
